cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FastqOptiFilter in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "FastqOptiFilter: quality-aware, FDR-controlled optical and proximity duplicate filtering for paired-end Illumina FASTQ files"
abstract: >-
  FastqOptiFilter removes optical and proximity duplicates from synchronized
  paired-end Illumina FASTQ files before alignment, using the lane/tile/X/Y
  coordinates already present in the read names. It applies no fixed
  spatial-distance cutoff: the length scale of duplication is estimated from
  each run, so the same command works on a patterned flowcell where duplicates
  spread over thousands of pixels and on a non-patterned flowcell where they
  sit within tens of pixels. Every run reports whether its own statistical null
  is calibrated, using two negative controls built from the data. The purpose
  is library complexity estimation, which optical duplicates corrupt because
  complexity estimators read the duplicate rate as evidence of resampling a
  finite pool of molecules.
type: software
